      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was relocated when the Fort Worth and Denver Railway bypassed its original site, making the railroad a key part of its history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarendon%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1898, Clarendon opened the Panhandle's first college, marking a milestone in regional education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofclarendontx.com/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Clarendon’s early settlers forbade alcohol, built a church first, and planned an academy, showcasing their commitment to temperance and education.",
